<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
<title>NaijaVote – Free Civic Education for Nigerian Voters</title>
<style>
  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  :root {
    --green:    #008751;
    --deep:     #005a36;
    --light:    #e8f5ee;
    --bg:       #f4f8f6;
    --white:    #ffffff;
    --text:     #0c1f16;
    --muted:    #4a6356;
    --border:   #c4dcd0;
    --gold:     #c9a027;
    --gold-bg:  #fdf7e3;
    --red:      #bf3b2b;
    --red-bg:   #fdecea;
  }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); padding-bottom: 72px; }

  /* HEADER */
  header { background: var(--green); color: #fff; position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100; box-shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,87,51,.3); }
  .header-inner { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 16px; height: 56px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; }
  .logo { font-weight: 900; font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: -.5px; }
  .top-nav { display: flex; gap: 4px; }
  .top-nav button { background: transparent; border: none; color: #fff; padding: 6px 13px; border-radius: 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 500; font-size: 13px; font-family: inherit; transition: background .15s; }
  .top-nav button.active { background: rgba(255,255,255,.22); font-weight: 700; }

  /* MAIN */
  main { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 16px 16px; }
  .screen { display: none; }
  .screen.active { display: block; }

  /* HERO */
  .hero { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--deep) 0%, var(--green) 100%); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 28px; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 24px; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
  .hero-bg { position: absolute; right: -20px; top: -20px; font-size: 140px; opacity: .07; user-select: none; }
  .hero-label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; opacity: .75; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .hero h1 { font-size: clamp(24px,5vw,36px); font-weight: 900; line-height: 1.1; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .hero p { font-size: 15px; opacity: .88; max-width: 440px; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .hero-btns { display: flex; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .btn-gold  { background: var(--gold); color: #1a0e00; border: none; padding: 10px 22px; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 800; font-size: 15px; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; }
  .btn-ghost { background: transparent; color: #fff; border: 2px solid rgba(255,255,255,.55); padding: 10px 22px; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; }

  /* STATS */
  .stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,1fr); gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .stat-card { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 12px; text-align: center; }
  .stat-card .num { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 900; color: var(--green); }
  .stat-card .lbl { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 2px; }

  /* SECTION TITLE */
  .section-title { font-weight: 800; font-size: 18px; color: var(--deep); margin-bottom: 16px; }

  /* TOPIC GRID */
  .topic-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(190px,1fr)); gap: 14px; }
  .topic-card { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; padding: 18px 16px; cursor: pointer; transition: all .15s; }
  .topic-card:hover { border-color: var(--green); box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0,135,81,.12); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .topic-card .icon  { font-size: 26px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .topic-card .title { font-weight: 800; font-size: 14px; color: var(--deep); margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .topic-card .summ  { font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }

  /* TAGS */
  .tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 20px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .5px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .tag-start  { background: #e8f5ee; color: var(--deep); }
  .tag-rights { background: #e8f0fb; color: #1a4fa0; }
  .tag-inst   { background: #fdf7e3; color: #7a5700; }
  .tag-law    { background: #fdecea; color: #8b2218; }

  /* BANNER */
  .banner { background: var(--gold-bg); border: 1px solid var(--gold); border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 18px; margin-top: 24px; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; }

  /* SOURCE NOTE */
  .source-note { background: var(--light); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 10px 14px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 24px; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* TOPIC DETAIL */
  .detail-card { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 16px; overflow: hidden; }
  .detail-header { background: var(--light); padding: 18px 22px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; }
  .back-btn { background: none; border: none; color: var(--deep); font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; padding: 4px 12px 4px 0; }
  .detail-header .big-icon { font-size: 24px; }
  .detail-header .topic-name { font-weight: 800; font-size: 17px; color: var(--deep); }
  .detail-body { padding: 24px 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 22px; }
  .section-item { display: flex; gap: 12px; }
  .sec-num { background: var(--green); color: #fff; border-radius: 50%; width: 22px; height: 22px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 2px; }
  .sec-content .sec-heading { font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; color: var(--deep); margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .sec-content .sec-body { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text); }
  .detail-footer { padding: 0 22px 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .btn-green { background: var(--deep); color: #fff; border: none; padding: 11px 24px; border-radius: 10px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; }
  .detail-source { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); padding: 0 22px 16px; }

  /* SEARCH */
  .search-input { width: 100%; padding: 13px 18px; font-size: 15px; border: 2px solid var(--green); border-radius: 10px; outline: none; font-family: inherit; margin-bottom: 18px; color: var(--text); }
  .search-subtitle { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .result-card { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 18px; cursor: pointer; width: 100%; text-align: left; font-family: inherit; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .result-card:hover { border-color: var(--green); }
  .result-top { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .result-top .r-icon  { font-size: 18px; }
  .result-top .r-title { font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: var(--deep); }
  .result-top .r-in    { font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); background: var(--light); padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 20px; }
  .result-text { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; padding-left: 26px; }
  .no-results { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 32px; text-align: center; color: var(--muted); }
  .popular-label { font-weight: 700; font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .chip { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 14px; font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer; color: var(--deep); font-weight: 600; font-family: inherit; }
  .chip:hover { border-color: var(--green); }

  /* QUIZ */
  .quiz-card { background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px 22px; }
  .quiz-meta { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .quiz-meta .q-score { color: var(--green); }
  .progress-bar { background: var(--border); height: 5px; border-radius: 5px; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .progress-fill { background: var(--green); height: 5px; border-radius: 5px; transition: width .35s; }
  .quiz-question { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .options { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .opt-btn { background: var(--white); border: 2px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 16px; text-align: left; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 500; font-size: 14.5px; font-family: inherit; color: var(--text); transition: all .15s; }
  .opt-btn.correct { background: #e8f8ee; border-color: #1a7a45; color: #1a7a45; font-weight: 700; }
  .opt-btn.wrong   { background: var(--red-bg); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }
  .opt-btn:disabled { cursor: default; }
  .explanation { background: var(--gold-bg); border: 1px solid var(--gold); border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 16px; font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .btn-next { background: var(--green); color: #fff; border: none; padding: 12px 28px; border-radius: 10px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; }

  /* SCORE */
  .score-screen { text-align: center; padding: 20px 0; }
  .score-emoji { font-size: 64px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .score-big { font-size: 48px; font-weight: 900; color: var(--green); }
  .score-pct { font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); margin: 4px 0 10px; }
  .score-msg { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; max-width: 320px; margin: 0 auto 24px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .score-bar-wrap { background: var(--border); border-radius: 8px; height: 10px; max-width: 300px; margin: 0 auto 28px; }
  .score-bar-fill { height: 10px; border-radius: 8px; transition: width .5s; }
  .score-actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .btn-outline { background: var(--white); color: var(--deep); border: 2px solid var(--border); padding: 12px 26px; border-radius: 10px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; }

  /* BOTTOM NAV */
  .bottom-nav { position: fixed; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; background: var(--white); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); display: flex; z-index: 100; }
  .bottom-nav button { flex: 1; border: none; background: none; padding: 10px 4px 8px; cursor: pointer; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 2px; color: var(--muted); font-family: inherit; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 500; transition: color .15s; }
  .bottom-nav button.active { color: var(--green); font-weight: 800; }
  .bottom-nav button .nav-icon { font-size: 20px; }

  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .hero { padding: 28px 20px; }
    .detail-body { padding: 18px 16px; }
    .detail-header { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <div class="header-inner">
    <div class="logo">🇳🇬 NaijaVote</div>
    <nav class="top-nav">
      <button class="active" onclick="showScreen('home')">Home</button>
      <button onclick="showScreen('topics')">Learn</button>
      <button onclick="showScreen('search')">Search</button>
      <button onclick="showScreen('quiz')">Quiz</button>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<main>

  <!-- HOME -->
  <div id="screen-home" class="screen active">
    <div class="hero">
      <div class="hero-bg">🗳️</div>
      <div class="hero-label">Free · Non-profit · For Every Nigerian</div>
      <h1>Know Your Vote.<br>Own Your Power.</h1>
      <p>Learn Nigeria's Electoral Act 2026 and the 1999 Constitution in plain everyday language — no lawyers needed.</p>
      <div class="hero-btns">
        <button class="btn-gold" onclick="showScreen('topics')">Browse Topics →</button>
        <button class="btn-ghost" onclick="showScreen('quiz')">Take the Quiz</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat-card"><div class="num">8</div><div class="lbl">Topics covered</div></div>
      <div class="stat-card"><div class="num">10</div><div class="lbl">Quiz questions</div></div>
      <div class="stat-card"><div class="num">100%</div><div class="lbl">Free forever</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="section-title">Start Learning</div>
    <div class="topic-grid" id="home-topic-grid"></div>
    <div class="banner">📌 <strong>Remember:</strong> Your vote is your voice. Every Nigerian aged 18 and above has the right to register and vote. Collect your PVC — it is your only key on Election Day.</div>
    <div class="source-note">📖 <strong>Sources:</strong> All content in this app is based on the Electoral Act 2026 (signed into law February 18, 2026), the 1999 Constitution of Nigeria (as amended), and verified reporting from TheCable, Daily Times Nigeria, and The Conversation Africa. Always verify with official INEC communications at inecnigeria.org.</div>
  </div>

  <!-- TOPICS LIST -->
  <div id="screen-topics" class="screen">
    <div class="section-title">📚 All Topics</div>
    <div class="topic-grid" id="topics-grid"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- TOPIC DETAIL -->
  <div id="screen-detail" class="screen">
    <div class="detail-card">
      <div class="detail-header">
        <button class="back-btn" onclick="goBackToTopics()">← Back</button>
        <span class="big-icon" id="detail-icon"></span>
        <div>
          <div class="topic-name" id="detail-title"></div>
          <span class="tag" id="detail-tag"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="detail-body" id="detail-body"></div>
      <div class="detail-source" id="detail-source"></div>
      <div class="detail-footer">
        <button class="btn-green" onclick="showScreen('quiz')">Test your knowledge → Take the Quiz</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SEARCH -->
  <div id="screen-search" class="screen">
    <div class="section-title">🔍 Search</div>
    <div class="search-subtitle">Type a question or keyword — e.g. "vote buying", "PVC", "INEC", "petition"</div>
    <input class="search-input" id="search-input" type="text" placeholder="What do you want to know?" oninput="doSearch()" />
    <div id="search-results"></div>
    <div id="popular-section">
      <div class="popular-label">Popular searches</div>
      <div class="chips">
        <button class="chip" onclick="setSearch('PVC')">PVC</button>
        <button class="chip" onclick="setSearch('vote buying')">vote buying</button>
        <button class="chip" onclick="setSearch('BVAS')">BVAS</button>
        <button class="chip" onclick="setSearch('election petition')">election petition</button>
        <button class="chip" onclick="setSearch('voter registration')">voter registration</button>
        <button class="chip" onclick="setSearch('INEC')">INEC</button>
        <button class="chip" onclick="setSearch('party primary')">party primary</button>
        <button class="chip" onclick="setSearch('ballot')">ballot</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- QUIZ -->
  <div id="screen-quiz" class="screen">
    <div class="quiz-card" id="quiz-container"></div>
  </div>

</main>

<nav class="bottom-nav">
  <button class="active" onclick="showScreen('home')"><span class="nav-icon">🏠</span>Home</button>
  <button onclick="showScreen('topics')"><span class="nav-icon">📚</span>Learn</button>
  <button onclick="showScreen('search')"><span class="nav-icon">🔍</span>Search</button>
  <button onclick="showScreen('quiz')"><span class="nav-icon">🎯</span>Quiz</button>
</nav>

<script>
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
// VERIFIED DATA — sourced from Electoral Act 2026
// and 1999 Constitution (as amended)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
const topics = [
  {
    id: "voter-registration", icon: "📋", title: "Voter Registration", tag: "Getting Started",
    summary: "Who can vote and how to register with INEC.",
    source: "Source: Section 9–15 of the Electoral Act 2026; Section 77(2) of the 1999 Constitution.",
    sections: [
      {
        heading: "Who is eligible to register?",
        body: "Any Nigerian citizen aged 18 or above who is of sound mind may register as a voter. This right is guaranteed by Section 77(2) of the 1999 Constitution, which states that every citizen aged 18 residing in Nigeria is entitled to be registered as a voter for elections to legislative houses."
      },
      {
        heading: "How do you register?",
        body: "Registration is conducted by INEC at designated centres. You must appear in person with proof of Nigerian citizenship. Your biometric data — fingerprint and photograph — will be captured on the spot. The Electoral Act 2026 mandates continuous voter registration, except that registration must stop 90 days before an election."
      },
      {
        heading: "The Permanent Voter Card (PVC)",
        body: "After successful registration INEC issues you a Permanent Voter Card (PVC). You must collect your PVC before Election Day — it is your proof of registration. The Electoral Act 2026 also recognises electronically generated voter identification with unique QR codes as valid identification for accreditation."
      },
      {
        heading: "Transferring your registration",
        body: "If you move to a new constituency you may apply to transfer your voter registration at any INEC office during officially announced revision windows. Corrections to your personal details can also be made at these times."
      },
      {
        heading: "Verify your polling unit before Election Day",
        body: "Before Election Day, use INEC's voter self-service portal at voters.inec.gov.ng to confirm which polling unit you are assigned to. Knowing this in advance prevents confusion and delays on the day."
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    id: "election-day", icon: "🗳️", title: "Election Day Rights", tag: "Your Rights",
    summary: "What happens at the polling unit and your rights as a voter.",
    source: "Source: Sections 47, 54 of the Electoral Act 2026; Section 143 of the Electoral Act 2026 (Secrecy of ballot).",
    sections: [
      {
        heading: "Accreditation — technology is now mandatory",
        body: "Under Section 47 of the Electoral Act 2026, technology is the only method allowed for voter accreditation. The Bimodal Voter Accreditation System (BVAS) verifies your fingerprint or facial data against the national register. You must bring your PVC or a valid electronically generated voter identification with a QR code to be accredited."
      },
      {
        heading: "Secrecy of the ballot",
        body: "Your vote is secret — this is protected by law. No party agent, security official, or INEC officer has the right to see how you voted or to demand that you show them your ballot paper. If anyone tries to coerce or observe your vote, report them immediately to INEC officials at the polling unit."
      },
      {
        heading: "How to mark your ballot",
        body: "Mark the ballot paper with a clear thumbprint inside the box next to your chosen candidate or party logo. Fold the ballot and place it in the ballot box. Voting more than once is a criminal offence under the Electoral Act 2026."
      },
      {
        heading: "Assisted voting",
        body: "Voters with physical challenges or disabilities may request assistance from a person of their own choice — other than a candidate or party agent. This right is protected under the Electoral Act 2026."
      },
      {
        heading: "Results must be transmitted electronically",
        body: "Under the Electoral Act 2026, results must be transmitted electronically alongside the physical collation process. INEC is required to upload polling unit results to the INEC Result Viewing Portal (IReV) in real time. You can view your polling unit result at irev.inec.gov.ng."
      },
      {
        heading: "Your right to observe the count",
        body: "Votes are counted openly at the polling unit immediately after polls close. Results are announced publicly and recorded on official result sheets. Party agents present are entitled to a copy. You have the right to remain in the vicinity and observe the entire counting process."
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    id: "inec", icon: "🏛️", title: "Understanding INEC",  tag: "Institutions",
    summary: "The role, powers, and independence of Nigeria's electoral body.",
    source: "Source: Section 153 and Third Schedule of the 1999 Constitution; Sections 1–7 of the Electoral Act 2026.",
    sections: [
      {
        heading: "What is INEC?",
        body: "The Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC) is established by Section 153 of the 1999 Constitution. It is the body responsible for organising, undertaking, and supervising all federal, state, and FCT Area Council elections in Nigeria. Under the Electoral Act 2026, INEC's mandate now also includes conducting referendums."
      },
      {
        heading: "Key powers of INEC",
        body: "INEC compiles and continuously updates the national voter register, monitors the activities of political parties, conducts voter and civic education, registers and deregisters political parties, and issues certificates of return to winners of elections."
      },
      {
        heading: "Financial independence",
        body: "INEC operates an Independent National Electoral Commission Fund established under the Electoral Act 2026. The Act now requires that election funds be released to INEC at least six months before a general election — an improvement from previous practice — to allow proper planning and preparation."
      },
      {
        heading: "BVAS and IReV",
        body: "INEC uses the Bimodal Voter Accreditation System (BVAS) for voter verification and the INEC Result Viewing Portal (IReV) to publish polling unit results in real time. Under the Electoral Act 2026, electronic transmission of results is now mandatory, not optional."
      },
      {
        heading: "Reporting INEC misconduct",
        body: "Any INEC officer who deliberately breaches the procedures for counting, announcing, or transmitting polling unit results commits an offence under the Electoral Act 2026. Citizens who witness electoral misconduct by officials may report to INEC directly, the police, or accredited election observers."
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    id: "political-parties", icon: "🏳️", title: "Political Parties", tag: "Institutions",
    summary: "How parties are formed, regulated, and held accountable.",
    source: "Source: Sections 77, 84, 88 of the Electoral Act 2026; Section 222 of the 1999 Constitution.",
    sections: [
      {
        heading: "Registration requirements",
        body: "Only INEC-registered parties may field candidates for elections. Section 222 of the 1999 Constitution requires that a party demonstrate national spread — it must have members and offices in at least 24 states of the federation before it can be registered."
      },
      {
        heading: "Parties are now corporate bodies",
        body: "Under Section 77(1) of the Electoral Act 2026, every registered political party is now a corporate body with perpetual succession. This means a party can sue or be sued in its own name, placing greater legal and governance responsibility on party leadership."
      },
      {
        heading: "Mandatory digital membership register",
        body: "Section 77(2) of the Electoral Act 2026 requires every political party to maintain a digital register of members containing each member's name, sex, date of birth, address, state, local government, ward, polling unit, National Identification Number (NIN), and photograph. This register must be submitted to INEC at least 21 days before any party primary, congress, or convention. Only members on the submitted register may vote or contest in primaries."
      },
      {
        heading: "Direct primaries only — no more delegate voting",
        body: "Section 84(2) of the Electoral Act 2026 abolishes the delegate system for selecting candidates. Political parties must now nominate candidates exclusively through direct primaries — where all registered party members vote — or through consensus. This is designed to end the practice of aspirants buying delegates' votes at congresses."
      },
      {
        heading: "Courts cannot stop elections",
        body: "Section 88(4) of the Electoral Act 2026 removes the power of any court to stop party primaries or general elections from holding while a lawsuit is being decided. Any legal dispute must be resolved after the election has taken place, preventing last-minute court orders from derailing elections."
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    id: "electoral-offences", icon: "⚖️", title: "Electoral Offences", tag: "The Law",
    summary: "Crimes that undermine elections and their penalties under the Electoral Act 2026.",
    source: "Source: Section 22 of the Electoral Act 2026 (vote buying); Electoral Act 2026 electoral offences provisions; reporting by TheCable and Daily Times Nigeria (March 2026).",
    sections: [
      {
        heading: "Vote buying and selling — now a very serious crime",
        body: "Section 22 of the Electoral Act 2026 criminalises vote buying, vote selling, and the illegal trading of Permanent Voter Cards. Anyone who buys, sells, or attempts to trade votes or voter cards — whether for themselves or on behalf of another person — commits a serious offence. The penalty upon conviction is a minimum fine of ₦5 million, up to 2 years imprisonment, or both. Crucially, a convicted person is also banned from contesting any election in Nigeria for a minimum of 10 years."
      },
